Concepts (credited by author and source)

WSJF (Weighted Shortest Job First)
  Source: https://framework.scaledagile.com/wsjf
  Author: Donald Reinertsen, The Principles of Product Development Flow (2009), as
  popularised by SAFe
  Used: the wsjf ranking (design spec 5.7).

RICE
  Source: https://www.intercom.com/blog/rice-simple-prioritization-for-product-managers/
  Author: Sean McBride, Intercom
  Used: the rice ranking (design spec 5.7).

One-way and two-way doors
  Source: https://s2.q4cdn.com/299287126/files/doc_financials/annual/2015-Letter-to-Shareholders.PDF
  Author: Jeff Bezos, Amazon 2015 letter to shareholders (Type 1 and Type 2 decisions)
  Used: the decision framework (design spec 5.3 and 5.8).

MIT CISR decision framework
  Source: https://cisr.mit.edu/
  Author: Sebastian, Weill, Haskamp and vom Brocke, MIT CISR, "A framework for determining
  when AI can make decisions"
  Used: the decision classes from reversibility, blast radius and ambiguity (design spec 5.8).

Verifiably Safe Autonomous Decision-Making (vGOAL)
  Source: https://www.kuleuven.be/
  Author: KU Leuven
  Used: the invariant table and its exhaustive test, without the model checker (design
  spec 9.2).

Error budgets
  Source: https://sre.google/sre-book/embracing-risk/
  Author: Google, Site Reliability Engineering, "Embracing Risk"
  Used: the error budget per decision class (design spec 5.8.1).

Brier score
  Source: https://doi.org/10.1175/1520-0493%281950%29078%3C0001%3AVOFEIT%3E2.0.CO%3B2
  Author: Glenn W. Brier, Monthly Weather Review, 1950
  Used: confidence calibration per decision class and role (design spec 5.8.1).
